WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.972
Start the Lang Graph state with only four fields: question, documents, steps, and route.

00:00:06.972 --> 00:00:15.836
Those four are enough to demonstrate shared state, retrieval output, step counting, and routing.

00:00:16.502 --> 00:00:20.419
Later, add query when query rewriting exists.

00:00:20.419 --> 00:00:23.279
Add score when grading exists.

00:00:23.279 --> 00:00:26.379
Add answer when generation exists.

00:00:26.379 --> 00:00:29.539
Add trace when observability is needed.

00:00:29.539 --> 00:00:32.589
Avoid turning state into a log dump.

00:00:32.589 --> 00:00:36.469
Large temporary prompts do not need to be persisted.

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:40.097
Secrets definitely should not be stored in graph state.

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:44.122
Minimal state makes the first graph easier to understand.

00:00:44.122 --> 00:00:49.072
Expand state only when the next node has a real reason to consume the new field.
